  "body": "Based on my understanding of promises, the only advantage of the following code block from `[[callPull]]` (which is the only observer of `[[started]]`) is that it may save one tick deferral, which hardly seems worth the added complexity:\n\n``` js\n  if (this._started === false) {\n    this._startedPromise.then(function fulfilled() {\n      stream._onPull(\n        stream._push.bind(this),\n        stream._close.bind(this),\n        stream._error.bind(this)\n      );\n    });\n  }\n  else {\n    this._onPull(\n      this._push.bind(this),\n      this._close.bind(this),\n      this._error.bind(this)\n    );\n  }\n```\n\nIt seems like it could be replaced with this:\n\n``` js\n  this._startedPromise.then(function fulfilled() {\n    stream._onPull(\n      stream._push.bind(this),\n      stream._close.bind(this),\n      stream._error.bind(this)\n    );\n  });\n```\n\n(sorry about all the `bind`ing)\n",
